  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://random-stuff.jakearchibald.com/popover-hint/\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9260b80b-a314-4d72-a175-51ad3110a768\n\n(includes sound)\n\nIf I open a `popover=auto` popover inside an open `popover=hint` popover, it hides the parent `hint` popover, then shows the inner `auto` popover (although it's visually hidden due to the parent hiding). This puts things into a weird state. Next time the `hint` is opened, the user sees the open `auto` popover, but a bunch of things like clicking and anchor positioning do not work as expected because the inner `auto` popover was technically opened first.\n\n[Here's where it happens in the spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-popover-attribute:opened-in-popover-mode-2:~:text=Run%20hide%20all%20popovers%20until%20given%20ancestor%2C%20shouldRestoreFocus%2C%20and%20fireEvents%2E).\n\nI couldn't find a test for this, but I saw another test mention \"You can't nest a popover=auto inside a popover=hint\", but, well, yes you can. If developers really aren't supposed to do this, it should fail.\n\ncc @mfreed7 @josepharhar @keithamus ",
